<h2 id="ha-ctrl-012-acceptance">Acceptance and evidence</h2>

1. Check distribution direction, source labels, kW versus kWh, period changes and missing/partial inputs without changing native quantities.
2. Inspect a gauge at minimum, maximum, out-of-range and unavailable values, and a pie with missing category data. No invented threshold or denominator.
3. Test reduced motion, keyboard access, non-colour cues and an actual value alternative for each named card/engine version. Record unresolved limits.
4. Switch away from civica and update an unsupported card. Native behaviour must remain intact and no Energy table, ONS label or adapter marker may be fabricated.

Record the integration/frontend version, browser, fixture or device, input state, expected result, observed result and evidence location. Source review and documentation checks are not live-device verification. Record unresolved native limitations explicitly; do not turn this checklist into an accessibility guarantee.

